# Laziness proof: $take does not force the tail thunk when n reaches zero.
# The third element of the seq is an error sentinel. After taking 2 elements,
# the recursive take(0, tail) PendingBuiltin returns Seq.Nil immediately without
# forcing `tail`, so the raise never fires (B-383 fix).
[collect [take 2 [seq 1 [seq 2 [seq [raise "tail past n should not fire"] []]]]]]
=== out
Dict({0: Int(1), 1: Int(2)})
